2026-09-10T18:20:20Z SURPRISE-ROW-OVERRIDE  3.0.0_SA_CVO~Z  reason=the L10 precondition arm mis-reads TO-IAM-t-3's status. TO_STATUS_RE (surprise-row-gate.py:124) is a FIRST-MATCH regex applied with .search() at :736; that order's PROSE at :32 reads "Carries NO <status> tag at all" -- describing a DIFFERENT document it was cut to investigate -- so the gate captures the word `tag`, finds it absent from TERMINAL_TO_WORDS, and declares a terminal order non-terminal. Measured on the same bytes: re.findall(r'<status>([^<]*)</status>') returns exactly ['complete'], and the order's own tag is at :165. An UNSCOPED sweep of all 18 task-orders/*.md reading the full <status>...</status> pair returns the histogram {complete: 18}, so the fact the rule protects -- every task order terminal, Andrew-direct LD-0521 "we do not route until the job is over" -- IS TRUE. The alternative of editing :32 is refused: amending a terminal order to satisfy a gate bends the artifact to fit the defect. Filed as row Z-S15, adjudicated at C-S16, routed to 1.0.0_SA_CTO~Z, and CARRIED IN THIS SLUG. Contrast: the same gate correctly refused this seat's NFRA_OPSEC202609 slug four hours ago and NO override was taken, because that order was genuinely staged.
